**Office Food Manager**

Product Requirements Document

Version 2.0  |  April 2025

| **App Name** | Office Food Manager |
| --- | --- |
| **Platform** | Android (React Native) |
| **Storage** | Local device only — SQLite, no backend, no cloud |
| **Author** | Internal / Personal Use |
| **Version** | 2.0 |
| **Date** | April 2025 |
| **Status** | Draft — Updated |

# **1. Overview**

Office Food Manager is a personal Android app (built in React Native) that tracks daily office meal entries for a group of colleagues, records the total cost once received from the mess owner, calculates equal cost splits, generates WhatsApp-ready messages, exports data as CSV, and syncs settled expenses directly to Splitwise. All data is stored locally on the device using SQLite — no backend or internet connection is required except for Splitwise sync.

# **2. Goals ****&**** Objectives**

- Maintain a list of people (name + phone number) for whom food is tracked daily.

- Log free-text daily meal entries per person with a full date (DD MMM YYYY).

- Record who paid the bill for a given day to correctly attribute expenses in Splitwise.

- Automatically calculate each person's equal share of the daily cost.

- Generate and share a WhatsApp message with the day's food orders to Rahul Bhaiya.

- Sync expenses to a pre-configured Splitwise group, updating existing entries instead of creating duplicates.

- Export meal and cost data as CSV for a user-defined date range.

- Keep all core functionality offline — internet only needed for Splitwise sync.

# **3. Target Users**

This is a single-user personal Android app. The user manages daily food orders for a group of office colleagues, collects the total cost from the mess owner (Rahul Bhaiya) via WhatsApp, and settles the shared cost through Splitwise.

# **4. Feature Requirements**

## **4.1 People Management**

The user maintains a list of people for whom food is tracked. Each person requires only a name and phone number. Splitwise user mapping is done once in Settings.

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Add Person** | Add a new person with name and phone number | Must Have |
| **View People** | View the full list of all people | Must Have |
| **Edit Person** | Edit name or phone number | Should Have |
| **Delete Person** | Remove a person (with confirmation) | Should Have |
| **Splitwise Mapping** | Map each person to their Splitwise user once in Settings | Must Have |

**Data Model — Person**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **id** | Integer | Auto-increment primary key |
| **name** | String | Required. Display name used throughout the app |
| **phone_number** | String | Required. Used for reference and potential future WhatsApp deep-link |
| **splitwise_user_id** | String | Nullable. Set once in Settings via Splitwise user mapping |
| **splitwise_user_name** | String | Nullable. Stored for display in Settings |
| **created_at** | DateTime | Timestamp of record creation |

## **4.2 Daily Meal Entry**

For each day, the user logs what each person ate. Each day has one meal event. Multiple people can have individual free-text food entries. The date is stored in full format including year (e.g. Thu 24 Apr 2025).

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Create Day Entry** | Start a new entry for a specific date (full date: DD MMM YYYY) | Must Have |
| **Add Meal per Person** | Select a person and type their free-text meal description | Must Have |
| **Multiple People per Day** | Any number of people can have an entry for the same day | Must Have |
| **Edit Meal Entry** | Edit a person's food description for a given day | Must Have |
| **Remove Person from Day** | Remove a person's entry from a specific day | Should Have |
| **View History** | Browse past day entries sorted by date descending | Must Have |

**Data Model — Day Entry**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **id** | Integer | Auto-increment primary key |
| **date** | Date | Full date stored as ISO 8601 (YYYY-MM-DD); displayed as 'Thu 24 Apr 2025' |
| **total_cost** | Decimal | Nullable — filled in once received from Rahul Bhaiya |
| **paid_by_person_id** | Integer | FK → Person. The person who paid the bill. Used for Splitwise payer attribution |
| **splitwise_expense_id** | String | Nullable. Stores the Splitwise expense ID after first sync; used to update instead of create on re-sync |
| **splitwise_synced** | Boolean | True if successfully synced to Splitwise |
| **created_at** | DateTime | Timestamp of record creation |

**Data Model — Meal Entry**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **id** | Integer | Auto-increment primary key |
| **day_entry_id** | Integer | FK → Day Entry |
| **person_id** | Integer | FK → Person |
| **meal_description** | String | Free-text e.g. '4 roti + rice + egg curry' |

## **4.3 Cost Management ****&**** Paid By**

The total cost for a day is entered once received from Rahul Bhaiya. The user must also select who paid the bill. This determines the payer in Splitwise — the payer is recorded as having paid the full amount, and all others owe their equal share.

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Enter Total Cost** | Input the total cost for a day | Must Have |
| **Select Paid By** | Select which person paid the bill from the list of people who have a meal entry that day | Must Have |
| **Auto-calculate Split** | Divide total cost equally among all people with a meal entry that day | Must Have |
| **View Per-Person Share** | Show each person's share = total cost ÷ number of people | Must Have |
| **Edit Cost / Paid By** | Allow updating cost or payer — triggers re-sync if already synced to Splitwise | Must Have |

**Split Logic**

- Cost is always split equally among all people with a meal entry for that day.

- Per-person share = Total Cost ÷ Number of people with entries.

- The 'Paid By' person is recorded as paying the full amount in Splitwise.

- All others owe their equal share to the payer.

- No custom or unequal splits are supported in v1.

## **4.4 WhatsApp Message Sharing**

After logging meal entries, the user can generate and share a pre-formatted WhatsApp message to send to Rahul Bhaiya to request the total cost.

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Generate Message** | Auto-generate message from the day's entries in the correct format | Must Have |
| **Share via WhatsApp** | Open WhatsApp with the message pre-filled using the WhatsApp URL scheme | Must Have |
| **No Contact Pre-fill** | App opens WhatsApp with message text only — user selects the contact manually | Must Have |

**Message Format**

The generated message uses the full date format and lists all food entries one per line, with no person names:

| **{Day} {DD} {Mon} {YYYY}** {Person 1 meal description} {Person 2 meal description} ... **Example:** **Thu 24 Apr 2025** 2 roti + rice + egg curry Puri + sabzi 4 roti + rajma + aloo |
| --- |

*Note: Person names are NOT included in the message — only food descriptions in entry order.*

## **4.5 Splitwise Integration**

Once the total cost and payer are set, the user syncs the day's expense to Splitwise. The app uses the pre-configured group from Settings. If the expense was previously synced, it updates the existing Splitwise expense (using the stored expense ID) rather than creating a new one.

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Splitwise Auth** | User authenticates once with Splitwise via OAuth 2.0 | Must Have |
| **Group in Settings** | User selects the Splitwise group once in Settings — used for all syncs | Must Have |
| **Person Mapping in Settings** | Each person in the app is mapped to a Splitwise user once in Settings | Must Have |
| **Sync Expense** | Create an equal-split expense in Splitwise attributed to the correct payer | Must Have |
| **Update on Re-sync** | If expense was previously synced, update it using stored splitwise_expense_id instead of creating a new expense | Must Have |
| **No Recurring Expenses** | All expenses are one-time — no recurring or repeat billing | Must Have |
| **Expense Description** | Auto-set to 'Office Food — {DD MMM YYYY}' e.g. 'Office Food — 24 Apr 2025' | Must Have |
| **Sync Status Display** | Show synced/unsynced status on each day entry card | Must Have |
| **Prevent Accidental Duplicate** | If cost or payer changes after sync, prompt user to confirm re-sync (update) | Should Have |

**Sync Logic**

- First sync → call POST /api/v3.0/create_expense → store returned expense ID in splitwise_expense_id.

- Re-sync (cost or payer updated) → call POST /api/v3.0/update_expense/{id} using stored expense ID.

- Payer = the person selected in 'Paid By' → paid_share = total_cost, owed_share = per_person_share.

- All other participants → paid_share = 0, owed_share = per_person_share.

- Only people with a meal entry that day are included as participants.

- split_equally is not used — shares are calculated and passed explicitly to support custom payer.

## **4.6 Settings**

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Splitwise Auth** | Connect / disconnect Splitwise account via OAuth 2.0 | Must Have |
| **Splitwise Group** | Select and save the Splitwise group for all expense syncs | Must Have |
| **Person-to-Splitwise Mapping** | For each person in the app, map them to their corresponding Splitwise user in the selected group | Must Have |
| **View Mapping** | Display current mappings with option to edit | Must Have |

## **4.7 CSV Export**

The user can export all meal and cost data for a selected date range as a CSV file, saved to the device.

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Date Range Selection** | User selects a start date and end date for the export | Must Have |
| **Export CSV** | Generate and save a CSV file to the device's Downloads folder | Must Have |
| **CSV Contents** | One row per person per day: Date, Person Name, Meal Description, Total Cost, Per-Person Share, Paid By, Splitwise Synced | Must Have |
| **Share Option** | Option to share the CSV file via Android share sheet (e.g. email, WhatsApp, Drive) | Should Have |

**CSV Format**

| **Date, Person Name, Phone, Meal Description, Total Cost (₹), Per-Person Share (₹), Paid By, Splitwise Synced** Thu 24 Apr 2025, Amit, 9876543210, 4 roti + rice + egg curry, 320, 80, Rahul, Yes Thu 24 Apr 2025, Priya, 9123456789, Puri + sabzi, 320, 80, Rahul, Yes |
| --- |

# **5. Non-Functional Requirements**

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Platform** | Android only (React Native) | Must Have |
| **Local Storage** | SQLite via expo-sqlite or react-native-sqlite-storage | Must Have |
| **No Backend** | No server, no cloud sync, no login required for core features | Must Have |
| **Offline First** | All features work offline except Splitwise sync | Must Have |
| **Performance** | App loads and responds within 1 second for all local operations | Should Have |
| **Data Persistence** | Data persists across app restarts and reboots | Must Have |
| **Single User** | No multi-user or account system | Must Have |

# **6. Key User Flows**

## **Flow 1: Add a New Person**

- Go to People tab → tap 'Add Person'

- Enter name and phone number → Save

- Go to Settings → map this person to their Splitwise account

## **Flow 2: Log Daily Food Entries**

- Tap 'New Day Entry' → date auto-fills to today (DD MMM YYYY), editable

- For each person who ate: select their name → type meal description → add

- Save the day entry

## **Flow 3: Send Message to Rahul Bhaiya**

- Open the day entry → tap 'Share on WhatsApp'

- App opens WhatsApp with the pre-formatted message (date + food list, no names)

- User selects Rahul Bhaiya's contact in WhatsApp and sends

## **Flow 4: Enter Cost, Set Payer ****&**** Sync to Splitwise**

- Rahul Bhaiya replies with the total cost

- Open the day entry → tap 'Enter Cost' → type total amount

- Select 'Paid By' → choose who paid the bill from that day's participants

- App shows per-person share = total ÷ number of people

- Tap 'Sync to Splitwise' → expense created (or updated if previously synced)

- Day entry marked as synced with Splitwise expense ID stored locally

# **7. Out of Scope (v1.0)**

- Cloud backup or cross-device sync

- Multi-user access or sharing the app

- Pre-defined menu / food item catalogue

- Unequal cost splitting

- SplitKaro integration (no public API available)

- Push notifications or reminders

- Automatic price detection from WhatsApp replies

- Analytics or spending dashboards

- iOS support (Android only in v1)

# **8. Technical Considerations**

**Platform: **Android (React Native with Expo or bare workflow)

**Local DB: **SQLite via expo-sqlite or react-native-sqlite-storage

**WhatsApp Share: **Android Intent / WhatsApp URL scheme: whatsapp://send?text={encoded_message}

**CSV Export: **Generated in-app, saved to device Downloads via react-native-fs or expo-file-system

**Splitwise Auth: **OAuth 2.0 — registered app at dev.splitwise.com

**Splitwise Create: **POST https://secure.splitwise.com/api/v3.0/create_expense

**Splitwise Update: **POST https://secure.splitwise.com/api/v3.0/update_expense/{id}

**Splitwise Participants: **Payer: paid_share = total_cost, owed_share = share. Others: paid_share = 0, owed_share = share

**Internet Required: **Only for Splitwise sync — all other features are fully offline

# **9. Decisions ****&**** Resolved Questions**

| **Feature** | **Description** | **Priority** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Target Platform** | Android only for v1.0, built with React Native | Resolved |
| **Splitwise Group** | Configured once in Settings — used for all syncs | Resolved |
| **Person-to-Splitwise Mapping** | Done once in Settings — no per-sync mapping needed | Resolved |
| **CSV Export** | Yes — export for a user-defined date range, saved to Downloads with share option | Resolved |
| **Re-sync Behaviour** | Update existing Splitwise expense using stored expense ID — no duplicates | Resolved |
| **Date Format** | Full date stored as ISO 8601; displayed as 'Thu 24 Apr 2025' (includes year) | Resolved |

